          "Build constituent service infrastructure visible to homeowners and renters alike: in a 55-45 district where education and income suggest high expectations for government responsiveness, active constituent service on school funding, local infrastructure, and permit processes demonstrates Democratic competence in a way that partisan messaging cannot.",
          "Avoid positioning college-educated professionals as a monolithic Democratic constituency: the 46.9% college-educated rate is high, but it is not 100%, and college-educated voters are not uniformly Democratic — engage this cohort on whether specific Democratic policies are delivering measurable benefits to their lives, schools, and property values, not on assumptions about their partisan identity."
