          "Lead with material economic security: housing affordability and tenant protections, healthcare access for a younger constituency (preventive care, mental health, reproductive health), and employment pathway development are the governing issues that activate this constituency's civic participation and determine whether they perceive government as serving them.",
          "Engage the ~12.57% demographic gap with specificity: identify the communities represented in that unaccounted portion of the population, understand their distinct economic and social concerns, and ensure that constituent service reaches them directly rather than assuming they fit into the majority-Black narrative.",
          "Build relationships with employers, workforce development programs, and community institutions that can create economic pathways for a 27.2-year-old median-age constituency—the representative's value to the district is not just legislative voting but active economic development brokering that demonstrates tangible opportunity creation."
