          "Leverage the college-attainment gap (30.8%) as an opportunity: this is lower than many urban districts, suggesting a constituency that values practical skills and workforce training over four-year degree pathways; align education and economic development messaging with technical education, apprenticeships, and rural job creation rather than abstract higher education access.",
          "Avoid taking the 36-point margin as structural safety: treat opposition engagement and challenger capacity building as ongoing concerns, particularly if economic conditions deteriorate or Native American voter mobilization increases around state policy issues; a 68-32 seat in Wisconsin can be competitive if fundamentals shift."
