          { name: "Treating Education as a Partisan Issue Rather Than a Fiscal Priority", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district with 29.3% college attainment and high median household income, school funding quality and educational outcomes are direct personal investments for the homeowner majority. Framing education as a left-versus-right ideological battleground rather than addressing the fiscal sustainability and competitive quality of district schools will alienate the college-educated, property-holding suburban base that actually determines outcomes in WI-HD-37. This constituency votes on whether their schools are funded adequately and managed effectively, not on national culture-war proxies." }
