          "Recognize that 67% is not a permanent floor: in a district of affluent, educated, mobile homeowners, candidate quality and demonstrated competence matter more than partisan attachment. Any Republican who delivers mediocre constituent service or represents the constituency poorly opens the door to a Democratic challenger who may not win but can erode the margin to dangerously competitive levels."
