          { name: "Partisan Realignment Based on National Culture-War Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "WI-HD-39's 70-30 Republican margin reflects local economic stability and homeowner priorities, not fervent ideological commitment to national partisan culture-war frames. Campaigns that emphasize divisive cultural or social issues over the material economic concerns of a 72% homeowner constituency risk shifting attention away from the issues that actually drive the district's politics. The constituency will support Republican governance if it delivers on economic security; it will not necessarily reward Republican candidates for their positioning on abstract cultural grievances." },
          { name: "Taking the 70-30 Margin for Granted as Demographically Predetermined", tag: "avoid", why: "A 70-point margin is comfortable, but it is rooted in active alignment between the incumbent's record and homeowner economic interests—not in demographic inevitability. Any candidate or officeholder who campaigns as though the 70-30 result is assured regardless of constituent service, fiscal accountability, or responsiveness to local economic pressures is misreading the district. The margin will hold only so long as homeowners perceive that their representative is actively working to protect their economic stability and property values." }
