          "Monitor cost-of-living pressures on the property-owning middle class: if property taxes, insurance, or utility costs spike faster than wage growth, or if local employers contract, the 30-point opposition will have concrete economic grievances to mobilize around—and the margin will narrow.",
          "Engage the blue-collar and small-business majority with specific policy fluency, not generic conservatism: the 21.3% college-attainment rate and 72% homeownership indicate a constituency that evaluates on whether government is delivering for working families and small employers, not on partisan tribal affiliation.",
          "Recognize that 70-30 is comfortable but not demographically inevitable: a challenger who offers credible economic relief to homeowners facing property tax or housing cost pressure could materially shift the margin in a district where homeowner stability is the political foundation."
