          { name: "Assuming Low Education Attainment Means Low Civic Engagement or Voter Sophistication", tag: "avoid", why: "The 18.3% college attainment rate is a demographic fact about pathways to education, not a measure of voter sophistication or civic engagement. Working-class voters without college degrees are fully capable of evaluating whether government is delivering on property tax relief, healthcare affordability, and wage support—and making voting decisions based on that evaluation. A candidate whose messaging or policy agenda treats non-college voters as unsophisticated or assumes they will vote on cultural signaling rather than economic outcomes will misread this constituency's actual decision-making criteria." }
