          "Lead on education quality and school funding sufficiency: with 38.7% college-educated adults and a 43.5-year median age, many voters have children in school and evaluate state representatives on whether education funding is adequate and stable. Property tax impact on education funding is the bridge between state policy and household finances—address it specifically.",
          "Engage affluent homeowners on fiscal responsibility and tax structure: the $95,375 income and 79.4% homeownership rate mean property taxes and healthcare costs are the primary state-policy concerns. Speak to property tax management, healthcare cost containment, and whether state budget decisions are protecting or threatening middle-class household stability.",
          "Do not assume this seat is held: a 51-49 margin in a district this affluent and educated is a warning signal that the incumbent has not consolidated support among the demographic majority. Any challenger who can credibly position themselves as more fiscally responsible or more focused on suburban quality-of-life issues has a genuine opening."
