          "Engage the education and workforce pipeline with specificity: the 35.2% college attainment rate is an asset and a competitive advantage for the region, but only if local education quality remains high and local employment opportunities exist for graduates who want to stay—be concrete about how policy supports both.",
          "Treat the 47% opposition as a persuadable constituency, not a base to be overcome: these are educated voters who made an active choice; understand whether their concerns are about cost-of-living issues, education performance, healthcare access, or broader economic direction—and offer specific answers rather than partisan positioning.",
          "Recognize that the 10.51% non-white population (Hispanic, Asian, and Black residents) is a material constituency in a district this competitive; their economic concerns around workforce opportunity, housing access, and healthcare are both constituent needs and an electoral swing factor in a 53-47 margin."
