          { name: "Positioning Climate & Environmental Policy as Secondary Rather Than Central", tag: "avoid", why: "A 71% college-educated, median-age-29.4 urban constituency with 53.2% renter concentration typically organizes around climate and environmental priorities with higher intensity than statewide or older demographics; relegating these to symbolic acknowledgment rather than centering them as legislative priorities misreads what this district's base actually cares about and risks mobilizing opposition from candidates who take climate seriously. Climate and environmental justice are not niche concerns in HD-77; they are central to how this constituency evaluates whether government is meeting the challenge of their lifetime." }
