          "Prioritize education funding and student debt policy: with 71% college-educated adults and a median age of 29.4, this constituency has direct interest in public university funding, student loan relief, and the affordability of higher education — positioning these as central legislative priorities, not secondary initiatives, demonstrates responsiveness to what this district actually cares about.",
          "Establish accountability mechanisms for constituent service: unopposed status creates risk of complacency; institutionalize regular town halls, constituent surveys, and transparent tracking of case resolution times to build the active relationship infrastructure that prevents future challenge from candidates who understand this district's values.",
          "Address climate and environmental priorities with specificity: a young, college-educated urban constituency typically evaluates on climate and environmental governance; specific legislative proposals on renewable energy, transit infrastructure, and environmental justice will activate and consolidate the most engaged portion of this district's electorate."
