          { name: "Partisan Polarization Framing in a Heterogeneous Urban District", tag: "avoid", why: "High-income, college-educated urban constituencies with significant racial and ethnic diversity respond poorly to divisive partisan messaging and abstract ideological positioning. These voters care about whether government is delivering results on schools, public safety, housing, and environmental quality — not whether their representative is winning partisan fights. A representative who leads with partisan polarization rather than concrete constituent service and fiscal stewardship risks losing the engagement of the educated, economically secure voters who form the core of this district's constituency." }
