          "Build a persuasion message targeted specifically at college-educated professionals earning $97,100+ income: this constituency is responsive to arguments about tax burden, regulatory overreach, and government efficiency when framed as practical governance failures rather than partisan ideology. The renter vs. homeowner split (40.4% renters) suggests distinct policy vulnerabilities on housing costs, zoning, and rental regulation that merit specific attention.",
          "Recognize that the 40.2-year median age masks a divided constituency: older professionals with substantial asset accumulation and younger renters with different wealth-building priorities require different messages about education, healthcare, and economic opportunity. A single campaign message that fails to address both cohorts' distinct economic concerns will underperform against a challenger who separates the messaging.",
          "Do not assume that Democratic tenure in a high-income, highly educated district is irreversible: upscale urban professionals have demonstrated a willingness to support Republican candidates when they perceive governance competence, fiscal responsibility, and respect for professional expertise. Any incumbent who defaults to partisan messaging rather than specific governance accomplishments is vulnerable to a well-positioned challenger offering a credible alternative."
