          "Engage the Asian American community (4.25%) and Hispanic community (2.78%) with specific constituent attention: in a 4-point margin, turnout and candidate preference shifts among minority communities are outcome-determinative, and their concerns around small business, healthcare access, and economic opportunity deserve direct policy engagement.",
          "Do not defend the 52% margin as safe: a four-point result in a district with deteriorating housing affordability, constrained wage growth, and two-thirds young or renter population is competitive, not secure — any candidate who campaigns this seat as though the current margin is a durable floor rather than an outcome requiring active constituent engagement and demonstrated economic delivery will find that floor crumble."
