          "Build explicit constituent relationships with the 27.1% renter population and the 8.53% Hispanic and 1.93% Black communities; in a district where these groups are demographically minor but present, their invisibility in the incumbent's constituent service creates an opening for opposition outreach.",
          "Lean into education and property tax policy with specificity: at $103,167 income and 42.4% college attainment, this is a constituency whose children attend well-funded schools and who care about education quality, tax fairness, and local government competence — these are the concrete issues most likely to move affluent suburban swing voters.",
          "Treat the 71% as a current result, not a structural floor — demographic change, education policy disagreement, or a national shift in college-educated voting behavior could erode this margin faster than in less-educated districts, so consistent constituent engagement and responsiveness are prerequisites for durability rather than optional."
